    {
      "name": "owned-table",
      "type": "registry:item",
      "title": "User-owned table (notes demo)",
      "description": "The ownership pattern: notes table with indexed userId, server fns that scope every query by the session user, zod schemas + test, page and /notes route under _authed. Rule for any lock you add (FOR UPDATE, advisory or lock helper): check ownership in the same query that takes the lock (join or WHERE on userId, or on membership for shared rows). Never lock by id and check afterwards: a non-owner would take the row lock and stall the real owner. Copy it for real tables, then delete the demo. After adding: run db:generate and db:migrate.",
      "dependencies": [
        "zod"
      ],
      "devDependencies": [
        "@types/bun"
      ],
      "registryDependencies": [
        "@john/auth-gate"
      ],
      "files": [
